          "Process_Text": {
            "original": "The LPBF fabricated samples were produced on a Concept Laser M2 machine with the laser power of 300 W, the scanning speed of 1100 mm/s, the layer thickness of 50 μm and the hatch spacing of 100 μm. The strip scanning strategy was employed in the fabrication process and the new layer was rotated 67° in the scanning direction relative to the previously deposited layer. All fabrication processes were carried out in an argon atmosphere. The H230 samples were subjected to hot isostatic pressing (HIP) heat treatment. The HIP treatment was carried out at 1175 °C for 4 h under 160 MPa of isostatic pressure, followed by argon cooled to room temperature.",
