        "Structure": {
          "Structure_Text": {
            "original": "The H230 sample exhibits severe cracking with a crack density of 2.81 mm/mm². After HIP heat treatment, the cracks in H230 are completely annihilated. Granular precipitated phases with an average size of 1.3 ± 0.2 μm and 0.45 ± 0.05 μm are distributed at grain boundaries and grains interior, respectively. The phases distributed at intragranular and intergranular are both W-rich M₆C carbides. The intragranular M₆C precipitated along the cell boundaries. The precipitate free zone occurs on both sides of the grain boundary. The number density of carbides in H230 was counted to be 0.52 μm⁻². The average grain sizes of H230 after heat treatment were 13.2 μm. The grain size of H230 (12.4 μm) remains essentially unchanged after creep testing.",
            "simplified": "As-printed: severe cracking (2.81 mm/mm²). After HIP: cracks annihilated. Main precipitates are W-rich M₆C carbides at grain boundaries (1.3 ± 0.2 μm) and intragranular cell boundaries (0.45 ± 0.05 μm). Grain size after heat treatment: 13.2 μm; after creep: 12.4 μm. Carbide number density: 0.52 μm⁻²."
